**Walk through the code**: Explain step-by-step what happens\n4. **Highlight a gotcha**: What's a common mistake or misconception?\n\nKeep explanations conversational. For complex concepts, use multiple analogies."}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto","style":{"padding":"16px","margin":0,"fontFamily":"var(--font-mono, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace)","fontSize":"0.85rem","lineHeight":"1.65","color":"#c9d1d9","background":"var(--code-bg)"},"children":["$","code",null,{"dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<span style=\"color:#38bdf8\">---\nname: explain-code\ndescription: Explains code with visual diagrams and analogies. Use when\n  explaining how code works, teaching about a codebase, or when the user\n  asks \"how does this work?\"\n---</span>\n\nWhen explaining code, always include:\n\n1. <span style=\"color:#e2e8f0;font-weight:600\">**Start with an analogy**</span>: Compare the code to something from everyday life\n2. <span style=\"color:#e2e8f0;font-weight:600\">**Draw a diagram**</span>: Use ASCII art to show the flow or relationships\n3. <span style=\"color:#e2e8f0;font-weight:600\">**Walk through the code**</span>: Explain step-by-step what happens\n4. <span style=\"color:#e2e8f0;font-weight:600\">**Highlight a gotcha**</span>: What's a common mistake or misconception?\n\nKeep explanations conversational. For complex concepts, use multiple analogies."}}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Test it two ways:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"code-block my-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"code-block-header","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded","style":{"background":"rgba(124,58,237,0.12)","color":"#a78bfa","fontFamily":"monospace"},"children":"bash"}]]}],["$","$L11",null,{"text":"# Let Claude invoke it automatically:\nHow does this code work?\n\n# Or invoke directly:\n/explain-code src/auth/login.ts"}]]}],"$L12"]}]]}]
